+  /// Where a floating window stopped growing is known from then on, as of a docked one (Controller+AskFirst.swift): docked, it goes straight to
+  /// the middle of its slot and not by way of the corner. It has told Arbor; it used not to be written down.
+  ///
+  /// All of the answer or none of it, for a record that is half, false or stale costs a move more than knowing nothing:
+  /// - both ways it was offered more, and both ways the answer is plain: it took that, or stopped short by more than any character cell. A
+  ///   terminal takes the whole cells nearest to the offer, which is neither. With one way on record a window goes to the middle that way, back
+  ///   to the corner to be asked the other, and to the middle again;
+  /// - no side that the screen may have kept short: where it stands, macOS lets a window grow no further than the edge of its display, and an
+  ///   app may carry a move out late;
+  /// - it has heard: a window grows about its middle, so one that has not budged is an app that hangs. Nor is one asked that has only just come
+  ///   out of the Dock or out of full screen, which may not be ready to take a frame (Controller+OnTheWayBack.swift).
+  /// And nothing about how small it goes: rounding up to whole cells looks like a refusal to whoever has not talked it down, as `place` does.
+  private func noteWhereItStoppedGrowing(_ id: WindowID, was: CGRect, asked: CGRect, took: CGRect) {
+    func isPlain(_ was: CGFloat, _ asked: CGFloat, _ took: CGFloat) -> Bool {
+      asked > was + 2 && (abs(took - asked) <= 2 || took < asked - SeenSizes.largestStep)
+    }
+    guard landsAt[id] == nil, took != was, isPlain(was.width, asked.width, took.width), isPlain(was.height, asked.height, took.height),
+      // One that grew as it was asked has said nothing that anybody needs: no record is begun for it.
+      took.width < asked.width - 2 || took.height < asked.height - 2
+    else { return }
+    let kept = sidesTheScreenKept(of: took.size, shortOf: asked.size, at: [was.origin, took.origin])
+    guard !kept.width, !kept.height else { return }
+    var seen = seenSizes[id] ?? SeenSizes(was.size)
+    seen.note(took: took.size, offered: asked.size)
+    seenSizes[id] = seen
+  }
